# MULEGUARD ML ARTIFACTS PLACEHOLDER
#
# This file exists only to preserve the directory layout in version control.
# It is intentionally inert and must not be used to store model artefacts,
# datasets, caches, logs, exports, binaries, pickles, notebooks, credentials,
# configuration secrets, or runtime state.
#
# Repository policy:
# - Do not commit model artefacts to this directory.
# - Do not commit training datasets or evaluation fixtures to this directory.
# - Do not commit raw customer data to this directory.
# - Do not commit raw complaint narratives to this directory.
# - Do not commit raw identifiers to this directory.
# - Do not commit ground-truth labels, synthetic labels, fraud labels,
#   scenario IDs, or fraud-ring IDs to this directory.
# - Do not commit subject-label pairs to this directory.
# - Do not commit secrets, tokens, passwords, API keys, private keys,
#   authorization headers, cookies, session identifiers, database URLs,
#   connection strings, filesystem paths, or environment files to this
#   directory.
# - Do not commit production artefacts or deployment bundles to this directory.
#
# Runtime behaviour:
# - MULEGUARD ML artefacts are process-local, non-durable, and bounded for
#   local prototype use only.
# - This placeholder does not imply persistence, deployment, promotion,
#   retirement, serving, or external model execution.
# - This placeholder does not imply production readiness.
# - This placeholder does not imply regulatory compliance.
#
# Product-safety notice:
# MULEGUARD is a synthetic-first investigative prototype. Alerts, risk scores,
# graph relationships, candidate money trails, entity links, complaint
# correlations, anomaly scores, fallback scores, model predictions,
# explanations, validation reports, and case dispositions are investigative
# leads or human workflow artefacts only. They are not proof of wrongdoing and
# must not trigger automatic adverse customer action.
#
# sentinel:muleguard.ml.artifacts.gitkeep:v1:inert-placeholder